adbd (1.0.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the Linux port platform-agnostic: resolve python3 through PATH,
    prefer bash with a /bin/sh fallback, make FunctionFS ownership
    configurable, and add a device-tree fallback.
  * Restructure sources under thirdparty/, usr/ and etc/; package the generic
    FunctionFS gadget manager and companion tools.
  * Rewrite the READMEs for users and add development guides under .github/.
  * Update CI to build amd64 and arm64 packages and publish tagged releases.

 -- wentywenty <2321901849@qq.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:50:00 +0800

adbd (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Include the generic FunctionFS gadget manager, systemd unit,
    modules-load and profile configuration in the package so it is a
    drop-in replacement for the old BSP adbd package.
  * Enable usbdevice.service at sysinit through the packaged unit link.

 -- wentywenty <2321901849@qq.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:40:00 +0800

adbd (1.0.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Install the scrcpy compatibility server and app_process shim.
  * Add android-compat command shims (screencap, screenrecord, input,
    getprop, setprop, wm, logcat, dumpsys, settings) under /usr/bin and
    /usr/lib/<multiarch>/android-compat.
  * Depend on ffmpeg, x11-utils and X11 input libraries for the shims.

 -- wentywenty <2321901849@qq.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0800

adbd (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Package AOSP adb master as a standalone Linux daemon.
  * Keep upstream sources in pinned submodules and apply one Linux port patch
    to a disposable build copy.
  * Support FunctionFS USB, explicit TCP/VSOCK listeners, Linux shell and sync.
  * Add amd64 and arm64 Debian builds and isolated protocol smoke checks.

 -- wentywenty <2321901849@qq.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0800
